{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "CSD19531Q5A",
 "kind": "mosfet",
 "manufacturer": "Texas Instruments",
 "title": "100 V N-channel power MOSFET (NexFET) in a 5 mm × 6 mm SON",
 "source": {
  "revision": "SLPS406B, May 2014",
  "pages": 13
 },
 "summary": "A single N-channel power MOSFET rated for 100 V from drain to source and ±20 V on the gate, in an eight-lead 5 mm × 6 mm SON whose underside pad is the drain. On-resistance is 5.3 mΩ typical (6.4 mΩ max) with 10 V of gate drive and 6.0 mΩ typical (7.8 mΩ max) at 6 V, both at 16 A; a full 10 V gate swing takes 37 nC, of which 6.6 nC is gate-to-drain. Its uses are the primary side of telecom supplies, synchronous rectification on the secondary side, and motor control. Avalanche rated; lead-free plating, RoHS compliant and halogen free.",
 "key_figures": [
